.cxx/

# Published APK — regenerated from the tracked source. Either by Android Studio,
# or by build-apk.ps1 / build-release.ps1, which live in D:\claude\android-build:
# those are workspace-local tools and are NOT part of this repository, so a fresh
# clone builds with ./gradlew instead (see README). An old debug APK cannot
# perform the functions of a newer source revision, so it is not versioned.
dist/

# Python bytecode caches (make_launcher_icons.py)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Release signing key. The keystore is the app's permanent identity — Android
# refuses any update signed by a different key — so it must never be published,
# and must be backed up somewhere outside this repository. Its password lives in
# local.properties, which is ignored above.
#
# The extensions matter: keytool now writes PKCS#12 by default, so a key
# regenerated under its natural name would be .p12 or .pfx and would not have
# been caught by the two patterns below. Leaking this key is unrecoverable, so
# the list covers the plausible names rather than only the ones used today.
*.keystore
*.jks
*.p12
*.pfx
keystore.properties
signing.properties
